ASSIGNMENT 6: COMPLEX QUERIES
===========================================================

IMPORTANT:
The following queries use the same simple database structure.
Where a question requires a relationship/property that was not
present in the original Assignment 4 sample data, the required
relationship is shown first so that the query can actually work.


-----------------------------------------------------------
1. LIBRARY DATABASE
-----------------------------------------------------------

a) Readers who recommended either of three books

REQUIRED RELATIONSHIP:
(:Person)-[:Recommended]->(:Book)

QUERY:

MATCH (p:Person)-[:Recommended]->(b:Book)
WHERE b.title IN ["Harry Potter", "The Alchemist", "Wings of Fire"]
RETURN DISTINCT p.name AS Reader;


b) Readers who have not recommended any book

MATCH (p:Person)
WHERE NOT (p)-[:Recommended]->(:Book)
RETURN p.name AS Reader;


c) Authors who have written a book read/issued by the maximum number of readers

Assumption:
Authors are Person nodes with an "author" role.
IssuedBy is used as the reader relationship.

QUERY:

MATCH (a:Person)-[:Wrote]->(b:Book)
OPTIONAL MATCH (b)<-[:IssuedBy]-(r:Person)
WITH a, b, count(DISTINCT r) AS readers
WITH a, sum(readers) AS totalReaders
WITH max(totalReaders) AS maximum, collect({author: a, readers: totalReaders}) AS data
UNWIND data AS x
WITH maximum, x
WHERE x.readers = maximum
RETURN x.author.name AS Author, x.readers AS Readers;


d) Books recommended by a person and read by at least one reader

Replace "Rahul" with the required reader/recommender name.

MATCH (p:Person {name: "Rahul"})-[:Recommended]->(b:Book)
MATCH (b)<-[:IssuedBy]-(:Person)
RETURN DISTINCT b.title AS Book;


e) Books recommended by a person and read by maximum number of readers

Replace "Rahul" with the required person's name.

MATCH (p:Person {name: "Rahul"})-[:Recommended]->(b:Book)
OPTIONAL MATCH (b)<-[:IssuedBy]-(r:Person)
WITH b, count(DISTINCT r) AS readers
WITH max(readers) AS maximum, collect({book:b, readers:readers}) AS data
UNWIND data AS x
WITH maximum, x
WHERE x.readers = maximum
RETURN x.book.title AS Book, x.readers AS Readers;


f) Publishers who have not published books written by authors from Pune and Mumbai

Assumption:
Books are connected to authors using :Wrote and authors have a city property.

MATCH (p:Publisher)
WHERE NOT EXISTS {
    MATCH (b:Book)-[:PublishedBy]->(p)
    MATCH (a:Person)-[:Wrote]->(b)
    WHERE a.city IN ["Pune", "Mumbai"]
}
RETURN p.name AS Publisher;


g) List voracious readers

Simple definition:
A voracious reader is a person who has issued more than one book.

MATCH (p:Person)<-[:IssuedBy]-(b:Book)
WITH p, count(b) AS books
WHERE books > 1
RETURN p.name AS Reader, books AS NumberOfBooks;


